Subject: [PATCH] bcm4908asus: skip subcommand when parsing create options

Pass the create subcommand as argv[0] to getopt instead of relying on
GNU argument permutation. BSD getopt stops at the non-option subcommand
and never reads the input pathname, breaking native macOS image builds.
Keep the command line and Linux image contents unchanged.

Signed-off-by: coolsnowwolf <coolsnowwolf@gmail.com>

--- a/src/bcm4908asus.c
+++ b/src/bcm4908asus.c
@@ -294,7 +294,7 @@
 	int err = 0;
 
 	/* Parse & validate arguments */
-	bcm4908asus_create_parse_options(argc, argv, &asus_tail);
+	bcm4908asus_create_parse_options(argc - 1, argv + 1, &asus_tail);
 	if (!in_path) {
 		fprintf(stderr, "No BCM4908 Asus image pathname passed\n");
 		err = -EINVAL;
